-- title:
--   The q+1 nodes of the descended supersingular model, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $A_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` of $k_0$ cut out by $A$, $\widehat{A_0}$ for its adic completion at `maximalIdeal`, and $\mathrm{res}_A$ for the residue map of a valuation subring. `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` is the subalgebra of $K_\ell$ of elements integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and for a commutative ring $W$ and $\pi\in W$, `UVCrossingModel W π` is $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, with `U`, `V`, `const` the classes of $u$, $v$ and of constants.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $q=3$; a nonzero modulus $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` which by `hW` is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in `ssJSet q`), and a chosen $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'`; and a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` along $A$ (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with a surjective residue map onto the special fibre field, a map on places, and the usual compatibilities), subject to the hypothesis `hR₀` that for a Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` the $R_0$-residue is computed by coefficientwise reduction along $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$.
--
--   **Base field and constants.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0\cap A$ such that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ (`hunif`), is Henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the approximation hypothesis `hκ` that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Further: a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ carrying the valuation subring $A_b$ induced by $A$ (`hAb`), whose maximal ideal is generated by a nonzero $\varpi_b$; $\xi\in k_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t'\in A_0$ equal to $\varpi_t$; and the tameness hypothesis `htame` that $\ell_g-1$ is a unit of $A_0$.
--
--   **Level and function field.** $H_1$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of `levelH q M'` — the kernel of the reduction of unit groups along the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'` — with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. $K_\ell$ is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ equal to the base change to $k_0$ of the $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ function field (`hKℓ`), an $A_0$-algebra in a tower with $k_0$; $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ is nonzero and has underlying Laurent series the coefficient embedding of `jq` (`hjℓ`); `hjK` records that `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in $K_\ell$, `hjC` that it lies in the chart algebra. Throughout, level automorphisms are the $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, i.e. those realising on quotients $f/g$ of integral-$q$-expansion modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ the slash action of `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` after an embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$.
--
--   **The point $y$ and the rigid model.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` containing $\pi_0$ (`hy`, `hϖy`); `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of `jChartFin` lies in `ssJSet q Ω` (no elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has a nonzero $q$-torsion point). The hypothesis `hover` (the moduli condition at $s$) states: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image is $R_0$-integral, has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` where $j$ does, and has $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, if the image of $g$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, then for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A(c)=s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0\text{-residue of }g)$ the difference lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same moduli condition is carried to $y$ by some level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and inducing $y\leftrightarrow y'$.
--
--   **The chart, the exceptional valuation ring, the deck group and the ends.** $B_t$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $W_t$ a valuation subring with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` (a conjunction of fourteen clauses, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra lies in $B_t$ and $B_t$ has fraction field $K_\ell$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal, and contracts to $y$ on the chart algebra; for any $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) of that residue field with kernel the locus of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with constants, equivariant for level automorphisms preserving $W_t$ through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c\neq 1$ for nontrivial $\tau$ coming from $\Gamma(q)$, and with the same scalar $c$ realised by a level automorphism whose matrix part is trivial; $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ receives the $W_t$-locus under some level automorphism of $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The deck data consist of $n\ge 1$ with $n\mid q+1$ and $n=2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ (`hn`), of $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with level automorphism $\tau_0$ preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`), of $m\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hm`), of $\zeta_c\in\widehat{A_0}$ with $\zeta_c^n=1$ and $\zeta_c^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$, of $a_0\in A_0$ with `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0\in y$ (`ha₀y`), and of a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. The hypothesis `hR7` (twelve clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ acts trivially on $B_t$ while $\tau_0^k$ does not for $0<k<n$, and every level automorphism of $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, transitively so, each end is preserved by $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; a $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-stable finite-type subalgebra $B_c$ exists of which every end is a localisation; a level automorphism mapping some end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end $O$ lies in $W_t$, is local and Noetherian, contains the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has every element congruent to a constant, and carries a crossing presentation $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m u$ with an isomorphism of the completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` over $\widehat{A_0}$ at parameter $\pi_0^m$ sending constants to constants, $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of $U,V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with the Igusa branch `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ going to a unit multiple of $V^e$, $e\ge1$, with $\tau_0$ inducing an automorphism $\theta_0$ scaling $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, together with an end-adapted discrete valuation ring $W_x$ and an end-adapted chart $B_x$ with their separation and pole properties; and finally a dichotomy for valuation subrings of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$ and containing the chart algebra with $y$ in the maximal ideal: such a ring either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. The hypotheses `hR9` and `hR10` provide elements of $B_t$ escaping, respectively, the valuation subrings of $K_\ell$ at which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental, and those attached to maximal ideals outside the level-automorphism orbit of $y$.
--
--   **Descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ consists of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$ (`hB₀`); $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ induced by $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist: a witness that the class of the coefficient embedding of `jq` in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`; a witness that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness that $\mathrm{res}_A(a_0)^q=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $K_0$ such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   (2) There is a subring $B_c\subseteq K_0$ which, for some finite subset $T$ of $K_0$, is the subring generated by the constants $\{\,x\in k_0\cap A\,\}$ together with $T$, and such that every node $O$ contains $B_c$ and is the localisation of $B_c$ at its elements that are units in $O$: $f\in O$ if and only if $f h=g$ for some $g,h\in B_c$ with $h$ a unit in $O$.
--
--   (3) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, and every $O\in$ `nodes`, there is $O'\in$ `nodes` with: for all $f\in K_\ell$ lying in $K_0$ and with $\tau f\in K_0$, one has $f\in O$ if and only if $\tau f\in O'$.
--
--   (4) For all $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $f\in O\iff \tau f\in O'$ for all $f$ as in (3); so the level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$ act transitively on the nodes.
--
--   (5) Distinct nodes $O\neq O'$ are separated: some $f\in O\cap O'$ is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$.
--
--   (6) For every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ such that $x\in A\iff x\in V$ for $x\in k_0$, and such that $V$ satisfies the moduli condition at $s$ — for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` which is $R_0$-integral, has non-negative order wherever $j$ does, has $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and whose coefficient embedding lies in $K_\ell$, the corresponding element lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A(c)=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue the difference lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ — one of the following holds: every element of $B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$; or there is a node $O$ with $O\subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   (7) Every node $O$ satisfies: $O\subseteq W_0'$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if $x\in O$; every $f\in O$ differs from a constant $x\in k_0\cap A$ with $x\in O$ by a non-unit of $O$. Moreover there exist an integer $E_0\ge1$; a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for some $v\in k_0$ with $v,v^{-1}\in A$; a witness $\pi_0\in O$; elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ of the completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal with `UVCrossingModel` over $\widehat{A_0}$ at parameter the image of $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that:
--
--   (7a) $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$;
--    (7b) $\iota$ sends each constant $x\in k_0\cap A$ lying in $O$ to `const` of its image in $\widehat{A_0}$;
--    (7c) $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$;
--    (7d) $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$ lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_0'$;
--    (7e) (Igusa branch) `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ with $\iota$ of this element equal to $w_V\cdot V^{e}$;
--    (7f) there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A\iff x\in W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; there is $t\in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; $c_x$ lies in and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$; for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` which is $R_0$-integral, has non-negative order wherever $j$ does, and whose coefficient embedding lies in $K_\ell$, the corresponding element lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, if its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs from every constant $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $c\in O$ and $\mathrm{res}_A(c)=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue by a non-unit of $O$; and every node $O'\neq O$ contains an element not in $W_x$;
--    (7g) there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ with: every $f\in B_x$ lies in $B_0$ (as an element of $K_\ell$) and in $O$; every $f\in B_x$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of $K_\ell/k_0$ at which $j_\ell$ has non-negative order; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its elements that are units in $O$; $B_x$ has fraction field $K_0$ (every $f\in K_0$ is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$, $h\neq0$); $B_x$ is, for some finite $T\subseteq K_0$, the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $T$; and there is $b\in B_x$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with $x\in A\iff x\in V$ for $x\in k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, and with the class of the coefficient embedding of `jq` lying in $K_\ell$, in $K_0$ and in $V$ and residually transcendental there (every monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ evaluated at it is a unit of $V$), if some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$ then $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the descent to the fixed field $K_0=K_\ell^{G}$, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ guard-prime frame and for $q=3$, of the $q+1$ ends of the blown-up rigid model of the modular curve at a supersingular point: it converts the ends upstairs into $q+1$ node rings downstairs, transitively permuted by the level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$, each with a crossing presentation $uv=\pi_0^{E_0}$ whose exponent records twice the width of the supersingular place $s$, an Igusa branch for `jqNModC`, and end-adapted valuation rings and charts. It feeds the assembly of the supersingular local data in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
